# What stays out of the .vsix.
#
# `vsce` packages every file under this directory that is not listed here, so the default is to
# ship the source, the Gradle build and the whole Kotlin/JS output directory - about half a
# gigabyte. What a user needs is `dist/`, the manifest, the icon, the licences and the two
# documents the Marketplace renders.

# The build, of which `dist/` is the seven files that matter. See `assembleExtension`.
build/**
.gradle/**
.kotlin/**

# The sources. The extension is compiled Kotlin; nothing here is read at runtime.
src/**
*.kts
.omc/**

# Source maps, which are excluded from `dist/` by the build as well - this is the belt to that
# braces, in case somebody copies a bundle in by hand.
**/*.map

# The two documents that are the repository's rather than the Marketplace's: the engineering log,
# and the notes on how to make a release. The page a user reads is README.md, and the Marketplace
# also renders CHANGELOG.md - those two stay.
DEVELOPMENT.md
PUBLISHING.md

# The vector original of the icon. VS Code renders `icon.png`.
icon.svg

# Editor and OS leftovers.
.DS_Store
**/*.swp
